  "name": "multiporox-automated-multi-material-porosity-analysis-tool",
  "notes": "This dataset contains files related to _MultiPoroX_, an automated porosity analysis tool for multi-material parts. It includes: The source code as a MATLAB file, the code as a PDF document, the user-friendly interface as a PDF document, exemplary analysis results of a multi-material sample (316L/CuCrZr) for demonstration purposes.\r\n\r\n__Used software:__ MATLAB® R2024b\r\n\r\n__Used parameters for the porosity analysis:__\r\n\r\n* __Resizing:__ None\r\n* __Histogramm Equal:__ 0.001\r\n* __Threshold:__ 65\r\n\r\n![Exemplary demonstration of an analysis result of a multi-material specimen (316L/CuCrZr)](https://data.uni-hannover.de/dataset/159b3c3b-b640-44ac-bcb5-8affc20632b3/resource/cfb27240-9488-4798-be75-ac95dd57784f/download/multiporox_multimaterial_defects_examplary_demontration.png)\r\n\r\nExemplary demonstration of an analysis result of a multi-material specimen (316L/CuCrZr)\r\n\r\n\r\n### References\r\nMeyer, I., Glitt, L., & Lachmayer, R. (2026). *Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – A porosity analysis of 316L/CuCrZr using an automated characterization approach.* Procedia CIRP, 36th CIRP Design Conference (CIRP Design 2026), 142, 558–563. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.procir.2026.05.308\r\n\r\nMeyer, I., Glitt, L., Lachmayer, R. (2025). *Comparative data of ImageJ and MultiPoroX* [Data set]. LUIS. https://doi.org/10.25835/l047b9xo\r\n\r\nMeyer, I., Oel, M., Ehlers, T., & Lachmayer, R. (2023). *Additive manufacturing of multi-material parts – Design guidelines for manufacturing of 316L/CuCrZr in laser powder bed fusion.* Heliyon, 9(8), e18301. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.heliyon.2023.e18301\r\n\r\n\r\n### Acknowledgments\r\n\r\nThe project ”*Additive Fertigung multimaterieller Komponenten zur nachhaltigen Energiewandlung*” was funded by the European Regional Development Fund (ERDF) and the state of Lower Saxony – Project number ZW 7-87011865.\r\n\r\nThe project ”*Major Research Instrumentation for integration of efficient effects in multi-material structural components*” was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG - German Research Foundation) - Project number 445707542.",
